This section covers how user-defined Context Objects are passed around in
callbacks.

## Overview

The Context Object is passed to call callbacks and event handlers through the
`context` property. The purpose of the Context Object is to attach additional
information to custom callbacks such as [Formatters](./formatters/) and [Tooltip Renderers](./tooltips/#using-custom-tooltips).

## Context Object Example

The example below shows how the Context Object can be used.

Changing the User Currency in the dropdown updates the Context Object
state. Note that the Context Object is used by the following callbacks:

-   The Y-axis Label Formatter, to convert USD values to the preferred User Currency.

-   The Tooltip Renderer, to render both the stock prices in USD and the User
    Currency (if applicable).

-   The Context Menu Actions, to log converted stock prices in the console.

